findings.problem:
The base building is a blank box with a level mark for the roof garden. Photos show features that frame the shaft:
- dark louvred mechanical volumes rising above the roof beside the shaft;
- thin cantilevered canopy plates on the airside;
- a continuous dark ribbon window along the airside face;
- on the landside, a large green-tinted curtain-wall bay directly under the glass ribbon.

The west facade is one uniform fill, 'mullion grid not dimensioned [unk]'. Several elements a visitor reads are not drawn:
- the departures canopy along the curb;
- its inclined support struts;
- the horizontally banded fritted wing walls, against the clear-glass centre section;
- the 'SAN FRANCISCO INTERNATIONAL' lettering on the centre bay.
The canopy struts give a measurable module that the README calls unknown.

The RCC is a plain box with a 'station tower 60 ft' tick. The two features a passer-by identifies are not drawn:
- the canted (outward-leaning) corrugated-metal upper wall over the board-formed concrete with ribbon windows;
- the free-standing cylindrical perforated-metal stair/elevator tower at the AirTrain station.

findings.evidence:
t1 (Basil D Soufi 2015, CC BY-SA 4.0, telephoto, near-level view from the east) shows 6 discrete parallelogram slots across the visible half. t2 (Famartin 2025) shows 5. The slots:
- start and stop on the horizontal seams at the top and bottom of the band;
- are 35-45 px wide in the 2x crop at 0.0367 m/px, i.e. about 1.3-1.6 m;
- are about 5 m apart at the middle of the band;
- all lean with their tops towards the NNE;
- each sweep about 20 degrees of azimuth over the 8 m band height. For example, slot 4 runs from +0.45 R at the top to +0.10 R at the bottom.
The band's levels agree with t1 (56.4-48.6 against the drawn 56.1-48.1), so only its form is wrong. In t3 / t4, 2-3 of these slots are visible on the NE flank left of the ribbon (t4 at x 290, 322 and 360 of 750). BT-02 B does not show them.

NAIP 2024 world raster, crop x -1000..-650, z 450..950. Positions are as imaged (not lean-corrected):
- roof wells at x -844..-825 / z 625..678, x -894..-844 / z 687..763, and x -922..-897 / z 772..812, with planting visible;
- bridges at about x -869..-834 / z 666..688 and x -919..-884 / z 753..775;
- skylight grids at about (-816, 700) and (-872, 806);
- PV rows along the axis over the whole length, and a large PV field at the south end (z 812..919).
The spec already records the wells (bab.roof_wells, pub / obs) and the PV layout (bab.pv_layout, obs).

d1 (Famartin 2025-08-12, CC BY-SA 4.0) shows the Harvey Milk Terminal 1 landside face:
- a two-tier fritted green-glass curtain wall with an irregular vertical-mullion rhythm (the 'redwood' pattern in t1c.landside_facade);
- a continuous glass canopy over the curb, with clear glass below;
- the 'Harvey Milk Terminal / Terminal 1' lettering;
- PV along the roof edge.
The spec describes T2 as a 'light metal-panel box with the "Terminal 2" sign and a glass entry wall'. None of this has a sheet.

spec sb_layout: 'cantilevered folded roofs to the WNW and ESE, each about 66.5 m beyond the spine ... 8 roof bays of 17.3 m ... doors on the WNW and ESE faces'. Its note adds: 'The Bay Trail photo ... shows roofs falling from a central ridge to both sides.'
l3 (BrokenSphere 2009, CC BY-SA 3.0; identification unverified) shows:
- roof planes falling from a central ridge;
- a row of repeated fold ridges on one half;
- tall door bays (dark panels) in the long face.
BL-03 has no roof fall, no folds and no door openings.

spec gh_plan_shape: 'crescent-shaped slab ... concave all-glass facade to the east; taller straight block at the north end next to the AirTrain station; 2-3-storey podium clad in dark metal panels'. spec gh_facade: 'dark stepped mechanical penthouse near mid-length; 4 corner masts'.
l4 (Gregory Varnum, July 2019, CC BY-SA 4.0) shows:
- the dark brown podium, about 3 floors, along the lower left, with large glazed openings;
- a narrow end module at the left with a different, horizontally banded curtain wall and the red sign;
- the dark penthouse above the roof right of centre, about 20 % of the face long;
- masts at the corners.

a2 (Pi.1415926535, Sept 2025, CC BY-SA 4.0) shows the pier with:
- a continuous departure-level glazed band at the holdrooms and light metal panels elsewhere;
- a long raised rectangular box and an elliptical raised drum on the roof, each roughly a quarter of the wall height.
